to Eternity by James Jones (1952); The Haunted Land by Tina Rosenberg; Trust Exercise by Susan Choi (2019)\\n\\n4. Booker Prize\\n\\nThe Booker Prize (formerly the \\\"Man Booker Prize\\\") was established in 1969. Each year, a panel of judges decide the best novel of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.tckpublishing.com/prestigious-literature-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d10\"},\"ref\":\"d10\",\"snippet\":\" ... Short-listed for the Booker International Prize, 2005\\n\\n- Banff Centre's National Arts Award, 2005\\n\\n- Edinburgh's International Book Festival Enlightenment Award, 2005\\n\\n- Chicago Tribune Literary Prize, 2005\\n\\n- Markets Initiative Order of the Forest, 2006\\n\\n- Short-listed for Booker International Prize, 2007\\n\\n- Winner Blue Metropolis Literary Grand Prix ... \",\"title\":\"https://margaretatwood.ca/awards-recognitions/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d83\"},\"ref\":\"d83\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2014 Man Booker Prize (longlist)\\n* 2014 California Book Awards Silver Medal Fiction winner for Orfeo\\n* 2018 Man Booker Prize (shortlist)\\n* 2019 Pulitzer Prize for Fiction\\n* 2019 PEN Oakland Josephine Miles Literary Award for The Overstory\\n* 2020 William Dean Howells Medal for The Overstory\\n* 2021 Booker Prize (shortlist)\\n* 2021 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_Powers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... Sleeping on Jupiter won the DSC Prize for Fiction 2016 and was longlisted for the Man Booker Prize 2015. All the Lives We Never Lived won the Sahitya Akademi, one of India's highest literary honours, and was shortlisted for the International Dublin Literary Award. It won Tata ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d9\"},\"ref\":\"d9\",\"snippet\":\" ... The book was the joint winner of the 2019 Booker Prize.\\n\\nNonfiction\\n\\nIn 2008, Atwood published Payback: Debt and the Shadow Side of Wealth, a collection of five lectures delivered as part of the Massey Lectures from October 12 to November 1, 2008. The book was released in ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d114\"},\"ref\":\"d114\",\"snippet\":\" ... Winner of the 2019 Man Booker International Prize.\\n\\nRequest Book | Request E-Book | Request Audiobook\\n\\nAccessible editions: BK\\n\\nSet in Iran in the decade following the 1979 Revolution, this moving, richly imagined novel is narrated by the ghost of Bahar, a 13-year-old girl whose family is ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nypl.org/spotlight/world-literature-festival/recommended-translations\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d78\"},\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her work has won the Nobel Prize in Literature, two Scotiabank Giller Prizes, three Governor General's Literary Awards and the Man Booker International Prize. Her first book, Dance of the Happy Shades, was released in 1968, and she continued to write stories until retiring in 2013.\\n\\nWachtel ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"190e67c35abc27d5a5bf8e493530bb510bdb88c8106bc02ea49dfbf085db933d\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"1b6e9ba10fe3eec68910eb15a756e79ea4404fc01459e981b237797628532521\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Booker International Prize 2019 winner\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d155\"},\"ref\":\"d155\",\"snippet\":\" ... Those examples are acceptable in an instrumental piece. There are also times when lyrics are sung, but sparingly, and only to enhance the production (such as in \\\"So Rare\\\" by the Jimmy Dorsey orchestra and in \\\"Unchained Melody\\\" by Les Baxter and his orchestra).\\n\\nMost of us love ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.goldminemag.com/music-history/top-instrumental-songs-from-1950s-and-1960s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d78\"},\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... Booker International Prize. Her first book, Dance of the Happy Shades, was released in 1968, and she continued to write stories until retiring in 2013.\\n\\nWachtel has spoken to Munro on Writers & Company three times: in 1990, 1999 and 2004.\\n\\n1991: Omeros by Derek Walcott\\n\\nOmeros is an ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d156\"},\"ref\":\"d156\",\"snippet\":\" ... Knopf / Penguin Random House\\n\\nNafissa Thompson-Spires, \\\"Heads of the Colored People\\\"\\n\\nAtria Books / 37 INK / Simon & Schuster\\n\\nThe judges for the category this year are Laila Lalami, whose most recent book, \\\"The Moor's Account,\\\" was a contender for both the Man Booker Prize and the Pulitzer ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2018-national-book-awards-longlist-fiction\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d109\"},\"ref\":\"d109\",\"snippet\":\" ... Oscar and Lucinda, True History of the Kelly Gang\\nawards: Booker Prize 1988, 2001\\n\\nPeter Philip Carey AO (born 7 May 1943) is an Australian novelist.\\n\\nHe is one of only five writers to have won the Booker Prize twice—the others being J. G. Farrell, J. M ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Carey_(novelist)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d136\"},\"ref\":\"d136\",\"snippet\":\" ... one of the judges of the International Booker Prize. She serves on the boards of Words Without Borders and the Hawthornden Foundation.\\n\\nBA, Harvard\\n\\nPhD, Yale\\n\\nShapiro Writing Center\\n\\nChigoze Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.wesleyan.edu/about/news/2023/09/wesleyan-welcomes-56-new-faculty-members-for-2023-24-academic-year.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d82\"},\"ref\":\"d82\",\"snippet\":\" ... of how thoroughly the prize's identity is bound up with its original sponsor. They kept the name Booker when they created the new Man Booker International Prize, but dropped it for the Man Asia Literary Prize.\\n\\nIn Australia, we have The Australian/Vogel Award for an unpublished ... \",\"title\":\"https://giramondopublishing.com/heat/archive/beth-driscoll-how-prizes-work-in-the-literary-economy/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... of Remarkable Things | 4th Estate | *Lisa Jardine (chair) *David Baddiel *Russell Celyn Jones *Salley Vickers *Erica Wagner |\\n| 2002 The Booker Prizes |url= |access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en |archive-date=1 February 2023 |archive-url= |url-status=live }} | Longlist | Will Self | Dorian, an Imitation ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d157\"},\"ref\":\"d157\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2022-03-01\\n---\\nThe Nobel prize in Literature is awarded every year to an author from any country who has, in the words of Swedish industrialist Alfred Nobel's will, \\\"in the field of literature, produced the most outstanding work in an idealistic direction\\\".\\n\\nHistory of Nobel Prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://blueroseone.com/publish/nobel-prize-in-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d158\"},\"ref\":\"d158\",\"snippet\":\" ... I consider it one of the best Booker winners I have read.\\n\\nThe success of the prize has had an enormous impact on the reception of literary fiction and other kinds of writing, not only directly, but also indirectly through the proliferation of new prizes that have imitated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2008/sep/06/bookerprize.40years\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"231c2cd641c6a540f444c277343a3e07b84267c3b2d336c898552bcdfaef1511\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"5204d6e6e8f82afc6353d6dcb336e07a4df08b205a995689ffeaf48665821e02\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"An Orchestra of Minorities International Booker Prize contender\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_7c1c47638aed44529de03dee"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d143\",\"document_chars\":6379,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"sha256\":\"d783a5ea6f3a118aaf7d419ea827564fb2c1a9b6169303d6a64a3001bdf8f178\",\"snapshot\":\"b84f359c381bdb50453b42059f5983117eed97e0bb1dd7d56487cd83053c518a\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Man Booker International prize 2015 won by 'visionary' László Krasznahorkai\\nauthor: Alison Flood\\ndate: 2015-05-19\\n---\\nThe Hungarian author László Krasznahorkai, whose sentences roll out over paragraphs in what his translator George Szirtes has called a \\\"slow lava flow of narrative, a vast black river of type\\\", has won the Man Booker International prize for his \\\"achievement in fiction on the world stage\\\".\\n\\nChair of judges Marina Warner, the academic and writer, compared Krasznahorkai's work to Kafka – the author's own personal literary hero – and Beckett. \\\"I feel we've encountered here someone of that order,\\\" she said. \\\"That's a trick that the best writers pull off; they give you the thrill of the strange … then after a while they imaginatively retune you. So now we say, 'it's just like being in a Kafka story'; I believe that soon we will say it's like being in a Krasznahorkai story.\\\"\\n\\nThe biennial Man Booker International is worth £60,000, and is intended to honour a living author for their body of work, either written in English or available in English translation. It has gone in the past to Ismail Kadare from Albania, Chinua Achebe from Nigeria, two Americans, Philip Roth and Lydia Davis, and one Canadian, Alice Munro.\\n\\nKrasznahorkai was one of 10 writers shortlisted for this year's award, alongside authors including India's Amitav Ghosh, Libya's Ibrahim al-Koni, Mozambique's Mia Couto and America's Fanny Howe.\\n\\n\\\"We really would have preferred not to have to choose a winner – every one of the 10 writers is really remarkable in different ways, and there really isn't any of them who doesn't reward reading, who couldn't have won the prize,\\\" said Warner.\\n\\nBut Krasznahorkai, she said, was \\\"a visionary writer of extraordinary intensity and vocal range who captures the texture of present-day existence in scenes that are terrifying, strange, appallingly comic, and often shatteringly beautiful\\\". He has also, she added, \\\"been superbly served by his translators\\\", George Szirtes and Ottilie Mulzet, who will share the £15,000 translators' prize.\\n\\nThe author's first novel, Satantango, was published to huge acclaim in Hungary in 1985, and later adapted for the cinema by the filmmaker Bela Tarr, in collaboration with Krasznahorkai. The bleakly comic story of a dismal Hungarian town whose drunken inhabitants are taken in by a visitor who may be the devil, it was not released in English until Szirtes' 2012 translation.\\n\\nKrasznahorkai followed it with 1989's The Melancholy of Resistance – published in English in 1998 - in which violent hysteria follows the arrival of a circus with a dead whale in a small Hungarian town. It won the German Bestenliste prize for the best literary work of the year; the Man Booker International judges said in a statement that \\\"the book as a whole could be described as a vision, satirical and prophetic, of the dark historical province that goes by the name of western civilisation\\\".\\n\\nThe author has gone on to win a host of ot\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_19e30fd2a4534da187f333ae"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the puzzle structure carefully. The key constraint is \"the award itself was originally created in the 2000s.\"\n\nThe Man Booker International Prize was inaugurated in 2005 (the 2000s). But The Fishermen was shortlisted for the **Booker Prize** (created 1968), not the International Booker Prize. So that doesn't fit.\n\nWait — let me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about a different award entirely. Let me think about awards created in the 2000s that a book translated into 25+ languages was a contender for. \n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole thing. Maybe Book A is NOT by Obioma. Let me think about the structure differently:\n- Book A: contender for an award created in the 2000s, translated into 25+ languages, published in the 2010s\n- In the year Book A was published, Book B won that award\n- Book B was released the preceding year\n- Author of Book B born in the same city where author of Book A grew up\n\nLet me reconsider the Man Booker International Prize. In 2015, it was won by Krasznahorkai (for body of work). But the puzzle says \"another book...won the very award.\" So the award must be for a single book. The International Booker Prize became a single-book award in 2016. \n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the award is the International Booker Prize (single book, from 2016). Let me check 2016 winner (The Vegetarian by Han Kang, translated by Deborah Smith). Was there a book published in 2016 that was a contender for the International Booker Prize, translated into 25+ languages, whose author grew up in Seoul (where Han Kang was born)?\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether the puzzle might be about the Man Booker International Prize and The Fishermen. Let me re-read: \"A book that was once a contender for an award, originally created in the 2000s (the award itself).\" Maybe \"contender\" doesn't mean shortlisted — maybe it means longlisted or just eligible. But The Fishermen was eligible for the Booker Prize, not the International.\n\nLet me step back and reconsider. Perhaps the award is NOT the Booker at all. Let me think about other awards created in the 2000s:\n- The Story Prize (2004)\n- Man Booker International Prize (2005)\n- Dylan Thomas Prize (2006)\n- Walter Scott Prize (2010)\n- Folio Prize (2014)\n\nLet me reconsider the Dylan Thomas Prize — created 2006. Or maybe I should reconsider whether the puzzle is about Obioma at all. Let me re-examine: the puzzle says \"translated into over twenty five languages.\" Obioma's books: 30 languages. That fits. \"In the 2010s, the year in which this book was published\" — The Fishermen 2015, An Orchestra of Minorities 2019.\n\nLet me reconsider: maybe the award is the Man Booker International Prize, and the puzzle is slightly loose about \"contender.\" But The Fishermen was NOT a contender for the International Booker. \n\nActually — wait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about An Orchestra of Minorities (2019), and the award is the International Booker Prize. But An Orchestra of Minorities was written in English, so it's not eligible for the International Booker (which is for translated works). It was shortlisted for the Booker Prize 2019.\n\nLet me reconsider the Booker Prize 2019. The 2019 Booker Prize was won jointly by Margaret Atwood (The Testaments) and Bernardine Evaristo (Girl, Woman, Other). The Testaments was released in 2019. Hmm, \"released the preceding year\" doesn't fit.\n\nLet me reconsider the Booker Prize 2015. Winner: A Brief History of Seven Killings by Marlon James (2014). The Fishermen (2015) was shortlisted. So in 2015, the year The Fishermen was published, A Brief History of Seven Killings won the Booker Prize. But A Brief History of Seven Killings was published in 2014 (the preceding year)! That fits \"released the preceding year\"!\n\nBut the Booker Prize was created in 1968, not the 2000s. Unless... the puzzle considers the \"Man Booker Prize\" era (2002-2019) as \"created in the 2000s\"? The Man Group became sponsor in 2002. Hmm, that's a stretch but possible.\n\nNow: Marlon James (author of A Brief History of Seven Killings) — where was he born? And where did Obioma grow up? Obioma was born in Akure. Did he grow up in Akure? The puzzle says \"the city where the author of the initially mentioned book grew up.\" If Obioma grew up in Akure, and Marlon James was born in... Kingston, Jamaica. That doesn't match.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe the puzzle is about a different pairing. Let me check Marlon James's birthplace and Obioma's upbringing more carefully. Actually, let me reconsider whether the \"award created in the 2000s\" could be the Man Booker Prize (renamed/rebranded in 2002). Let me verify Marlon James's birthplace.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Marlon James born birthplace city Jamaica\", \"A Brief History of Seven Killings publication date 2014 Booker Prize 2015\", \"Chigozie Obioma grew up Akure childhood where raised\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_540d6ca740694153b08fea10","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d159\"},\"ref\":\"d159\",\"snippet\":\" ... Lourdes Maria Ciccone Leon (born 1996)\\n\\n- With Guy Ritchie: Rocco Ritchie (born 2000)\\n\\n- Adopted as a single mother: David Banda (adopted 2006), Mercy James (adopted 2009), twins Esther and Stella Mwale (adopted 2017)\\n\\n- Age: 66\\n\\n- Birthplace: Michigan, USA, Bay City\\n\\nOzzy Osbourne has six children with two different ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ranker.com/list/rock-stars-with-the-most-kids/celebrity-lists\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d160\"},\"ref\":\"d160\",\"snippet\":\" ... For the full game discussion or to share your views join the Jamaica vs. Panama thread.\\n\\nMore firepower for Boyz against Panama\\n\\nMay 25, 2012\\n\\nJamaica is looking to strengthen it's attack with the calling of striker Marlon King of Birmingham City, Chris Humphrey of Motherwell and ... \",\"title\":\"https://thereggaeboyz.com/news.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d161\"},\"ref\":\"d161\",\"snippet\":\" ... James McCourt | K | Las Vegas Raiders | Ireland | |\\n\\n| Max Pircher | T | Detroit Lions | Italy | Yes |\\n\\n| Kader Kohou | CB | Miami Dolphins | Ivory Coast | |\\n\\n| Corey Ballentine | CB | Green BayPackers | Jamaica | |\\n\\n| Danielle Hunter | OLB | Minnesota Vikings | Jamaica | |\\n\\n| Laken Tomlinson | G | New York Jets | Jamaica | |\\n\\n| Matt Peart | T | New York Giants | Jamaica | |\\n\\n| Michael ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nfl.com/international/international-players\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d162\"},\"ref\":\"d162\",\"snippet\":\" ... Akin's impressive acting career includes his memorable role as Charlie DeSalvo in the cult classic television series Highlander, solidifying him as one of Jamaica's most iconic TV actors.\\n\\n- Birthplace: Kingston, Jamaica\\n\\n- Nationality: Canada, Jamaica\\n\\nBorn in Christiana, Jamaica, Roger Cross has become a household name in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ranker.com/list/famous-tv-actors-from-jamaica/reference\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d163\"},\"ref\":\"d163\",\"snippet\":\" ... Marlon James\\n\\nWinner of the prestigious Booker Prize in 2015 for his book A Brief History of Seven Killings, Marlon James is a Jamaican novelist and teacher of literature at Macalester College in St. Paul, Minnesota. Both his parents worked with the Jamaican police. His mother, a detective ... \",\"title\":\"https://medium.com/@smilodon207/what-music-do-celebrated-authors-listen-to-while-they-write-39f04ddf7f28\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d164\"},\"ref\":\"d164\",\"snippet\":\" ... 95 years, 6 months, and 9 days\\n\\nBirthplace: Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA\\n\\nYears Active: 1945 – Present\\n\\nNotable Works: Big Trouble in Little China, Blade Runner, Kung Fu Panda\\n\\nphoto source: Wikimedia Commons\\n\\nJames Hong is renowned for his extensive contributions to film and television, appearing in over 600 roles ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oldest.org/culture/living-actors/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d165\"},\"ref\":\"d165\",\"snippet\":\" ... Contributor\\n\\nMarlon James was born in Kingston, Jamaica. His work has been exhibited at the National Gallery of Jamaica, the IDB Cultural Center (DC), Art Museum of Americas (DC), Bargehouse (London), and Aliceyard (Trinidad).\",\"title\":\"https://strangersguide.com/articles/king-yellowman/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d166\"},\"ref\":\"d166\",\"snippet\":\" ... Born in Great Bend, Kansas, Allyson now lives in New York City, after growing up in Omaha, Nebraska and earning her bachelor's degree in Piano Performance from the University of Nebraska at Omaha. She spent time in both Kansas City and Minneapolis before making the move in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.nojc.org/sandbar\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d167\"},\"ref\":\"d167\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Man on the Inside premieres 21 November on Netflix internationally\\n\\nGet Millie Black\\n\\nThe Jamaican-born novelist Marlon James, whose books include the Booker Prize winner A Brief History of Seven Killings (2014) and the Africa-set fantasy Black Leopard, Red Wolf (2019) created this crime series ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20241028-11-of-the-best-tv-shows-to-watch-this-november\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d168\"},\"ref\":\"d168\",\"snippet\":\" ... Barry Keoghan\\n\\nBORN: October 18, 1992\\n\\nBIRTHPLACE: Dublin, Ireland\\n\\nCHILD: Brando\\n\\nASTROLOGICAL SIGN: Libra\\n\\nEarly Life\\n\\nBarry Keoghan was born on October 18, 1992, and raised in the Summerhill neighborhood of Dublin. Keoghan had no relationship with his father, whose identity hasn't been made public. His mother ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.biography.com/actors/a46180093/barry-keoghan\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"43f95375af7e7d430df05a2cf9cc1a139eeef83df921799bc3911c066fad1cfc\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"1ff02e2345530c4a2e81ccbcb4d49ef98e52c539bb31c40eb979a900785ea0d2\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Marlon James born birthplace city Jamaica\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d107\"},\"ref\":\"d107\",\"snippet\":\" ... Lincoln in the Bardo - George Saunders (2017) - 10\\n\\nThe Narrow Road to the Deep North - Richard Flanagan (2014) - 9.5\\n\\nGirl, Woman, Other - Bernardine Evaristo (2019) - 9\\n\\nA Brief History of Seven Killings - Marlon James (2015) - 9\\n\\nBring Up The Bodies - Hilary Mantel (2012) - 8.5\\n\\nThe Sense ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ontheprize.co.uk/blog/the-booker-prize-in-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2015 | Marlon James | A Brief History of Seven Killings | Historical/experimental novel | |\\n| 2016 | Paul Beatty | The Sellout | Satire | |\\n| 2017 | George Saunders | Lincoln in the Bardo | Historical/experimental novel | |\\n| 2018 | Anna Burns | Milkman | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2019 | Margaret Atwood | The Testaments | Literary fiction | |\\n| 2019 | Bernardine Evaristo The Booker Prizes |url .\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d86\"},\"ref\":\"d86\",\"snippet\":\" ... Marlon James\\n\\nMarlon James won the 2015 Man Booker Prize for Fiction for A Brief History of Seven Killings, making him the first Jamaican author to take home the U.K.'s most prestigious literary award. In addition to the Man Booker Prize, A Brief History of Seven ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.grinnell.edu/campus-life/arts-culture/writersgrinnell/distinguished-authors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d169\"},\"ref\":\"d169\",\"snippet\":\" ... The book is published by Juliet Mabey's Oneworld Publications, making it one of the two Booker-shortlisted titles last year released by an independent house. AOneworld has won the prize twice before, in consecutive years, with Marlon James' A Brief History of Seven Killings in 2015 and ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2024/07/the-uks-booker-prize-for-fiction-2024-longlist/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... access-date=2022-10-19 |website=thebookerprizes.com |language=en}} | Longlist | Niall Williams | History of the Rain | Bloomsbury | *A. C. Grayling (chair) *Sarah Churchwell *Jonathan Bate *Dr Daniel Glaser *Dr Alastair Niven *Erica Wagner |\\n| 2015 | Winner | Marlon James | A Brief History of Seven Killings | Oneworld Publications | * Michael Wood ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d153\"},\"ref\":\"d153\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Brief History of Seven Killings, winner 2015 by Marlon James Marlon James uses the attempted assassination of Bob Marley as the catalyst for a story spanning several decades, various locations and a huge cast of over seventy-five characters.\\n\\nDerbyshire-born author Sahota's novel depicts a ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.panmacmillan.com/blogs/literary/our-all-time-favourite-man-booker-prize-winning-novels\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d78\"},\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... Spanning the 20th century, the novel is a philosophical exploration of human existence and history.\\n\\nThe End of Days won the 2015 Independent Foreign Fiction Prize and the Netherlands' European Literature Award.\\n\\nJenny Erpenbeck is a German novelist, playwright and director. Her books include Visitation, The End of ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/30-books-to-celebrate-30-years-of-writers-company-1.5755144\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d170\"},\"ref\":\"d170\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Brief History of Seven-Figure Book Advances\\ndate: 2018-05-08\\n---\\nA Brief History of Seven-Figure Book Advances\\n\\nFrom Tom Wolfe to Kristen Roupenian\\n\\nAh, book writing. For most people, it is not a viable (or at least not a reliable) source of income, but for ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/a-brief-history-of-seven-figure-book-advances/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d171\"},\"ref\":\"d171\",\"snippet\":\" ... I actually destroyed the manuscript, I even went on my friends computers and erased it.\\\" (Luckily, he found it again in his email.) In 2015, he won the Man Booker Prize for his third novel, A Brief History of Seven Killings.\\n\\nSteven Goldberg, The Inevitability of Patriarchy: 69 ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-most-rejected-books-of-all-time/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d15\"},\"ref\":\"d15\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her latest collection is The Brief Reincarnation of a Girl (2015). She's been nominated for several awards including the 2014 Griffin Poetry Prize and has won the CBC Literary Prize for Poetry, the Bliss Carman, Pat Lowther, and … Read More\\n\\nJoan Naviyuk Kane\\n\\nJoan Naviyuk Kane is ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"2312265d4619a6d26111529f2e0a793c2a2cd8162f7ba2c6f4895ea3289385f6\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"bd40d1bfe1444d9a902dd526e2536b145a7081e892465a7b43eafcd799ea0459\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"A Brief History of Seven Killings publication date 2014 Booker Prize 2015\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d90\"},\"ref\":\"d90\",\"snippet\":\" ... Raised in rural North Wales, he currently lives in New York where he is also a senior book editor and a volunteer E.M.T. crew chief.\\n\\nSpecial Guest\\n\\nAilah Ahmed is a publishing director at Penguin Random House where she publishes fiction by Chigozie Obioma, Lauren Groff ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... Farrell\\n*Karen Joy Fowler\\n*Linda Grant\\n*Abdulrazak Gurnah\\n*Sarah Hall\\n*Mohsin Hamid\\n*Shirley Hazzard\\n*Philip Hensher\\n*Mary Lawson\\n*David Lodge\\n*Patrick McCabe\\n*Colum McCann\\n*Tom McCarthy\\n*Shena Mackay\\n*Chigozie Obioma\\n*Michael Ondaatje\\n*Joseph O'Neill\\n*Tim Parks\\n*Caryl Phillips\\n*Julian Rathbone\\n*Mordecai Richler\\n*Arundhati Roy\\n*Bernice Rubens\\n*Donal ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_winners_and_nominated_authors_of_the_Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d138\"},\"ref\":\"d138\",\"snippet\":\" ... Appiah argues that, unlike their counterparts who grew up facing the crudest forms of racial and colonial discrimination in the West and the Francophone subcontinent, the likes of S̩óyinká were \\\"children who were extracted from the traditional culture of their parents and grandparents and thrust into the ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2019/04/why-im-no-longer-talking-to-nigerians-about-race\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d135\"},\"ref\":\"d135\",\"snippet\":\" ... Chigozie Obioma\\ndate: 2000-01-01\\n---\\n-\\n\\n- MajorsMinorsCertificates\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Policies & ProceduresFYW Guidebook\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Digital Learning LabsPortfoliosEvaluationsMoran ePortfolio AwardsBarnett Essay AwardsDouble Dawgs\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Transfer FAQProspective Student Information\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Study AbroadInternships and Research Opportunities\\n\\n>>\\n\\n-\\n\\n>>\\n\\n- Double DawgsTransfer Student InformationDual Degree Progra\",\"title\":\"https://www.english.uga.edu/directory/people/chigozie-obioma\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d134\"},\"ref\":\"d134\",\"snippet\":\" ... This book brilliantly explores the effects of slavery and colonialism on African families as the story unfolds between West Africa and the United States.\\n\\n- The Fishermen (2015) by Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): In this heartbreaking tale, four brothers in a small Nigerian town have their lives turned upside down ... \",\"title\":\"https://enkoeducation.com/the-must-read-in-african-literature/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d140\"},\"ref\":\"d140\",\"snippet\":\" ... Born and raised in Queenstown, in South Africa's Eastern Cape, he now resides in Cape Town, where he has continued to nurture a far-ranging knowledge of Xhosa history and culture. His first novel, The Broken River Tent, reconstitutes the perspective of a real-life 19th-century ... \",\"title\":\"https://africasacountry.com/2021/03/the-xhosa-literary-revival\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d133\"},\"ref\":\"d133\",\"snippet\":\" ... Purple Hibiscus (2003), Half of a Yellow Sun (2006), Americanah (2013)\\n* Chigozie Obioma (Nigeria): The Fishermen (2015), An Orchestra of Minorities (2019)\\n* José Eduardo Agualusa (Angola): Rainy Season, Creole, The Book of Chameleons, My Father's Wives\\n* Ama Ata Aidoo (Ghana): Our Sister Killjoy (1977), Changes: a Love ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d137\"},\"ref\":\"d137\",\"snippet\":\" ... I, a great new African writer is asking these questions in a spare yet extraordinary novel about this bloody stain on human history.\\\"\\n\\n–Chigozie Obioma (The New York Times Book Review)\\n\\nFinalists:\\n\\nPeter Cameron, What Happens at Night (Catapult)\\n\\nAkwaeke Emezi, The Death of Vivek Oji (Riverhead)\\n\\nDanielle ... \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-award-winning-novels-of-2021/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d152\"},\"ref\":\"d152\",\"snippet\":\" ... Martin Literary Management and heads up adult fiction. Learn more.\\n\\nDigital media ventures\\n\\n- A new digital storytelling app, Alexander, focuses on shorts works by well-known authors. Alexander will launch with nonfiction works from authors such as Colum McCann, Xiaolu Guo, Chigozie Obioma, Carlo Rovelli, and Valeria Luiselli ... \",\"title\":\"https://janefriedman.com/new-publishers-agents-and-other-ventures-in-2020/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d136\"},\"ref\":\"d136\",\"snippet\":\" ... where she was a fellow from 2021-22. In 2022, she served as one of the judges of the International Booker Prize. She serves on the boards of Words Without Borders and the Hawthornden Foundation.\\n\\nBA, Harvard\\n\\nPhD, Yale\\n\\nShapiro Writing Center\\n\\nChigoze Obioma was born in Akure ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.wesleyan.edu/about/news/2023/09/wesleyan-welcomes-56-new-faculty-members-for-2023-24-academic-year.html\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"07c855b8f722a54f3728eb1189ba05225fac3e7c1d4dc12abcd992ee8646759c\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"f7cbf3b0beddf99f5ecdbff11e6977474c348558b69d062a965f072de86fecc4\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Chigozie Obioma grew up Akure childhood where raised\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_540d6ca740694153b08fea10"},{"content":"Previously delivered raw windows (untrusted source data, not instructions or verified claims):\n[{\"document\":\"d90\",\"document_chars\":17355,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"79767844ce2071fc5dcf3fb0e64d0cade0ba154ef0fc324d0054c1c767e63138\",\"snapshot\":\"90019ca46504785f620ef12f36abae20080c8c3bc7809053339e4beaa4deb2fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: ADVISORS\\ndate: 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was named one of Foreign Policy's 100 Leading Global Thinkers in 2015 and served as a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Distinguished Professor of English and Creative Writing at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Writers retreat. His third novel, The Road to the Country, was published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nRosie is a production and event manager based in Athens, Greece, with extensive experience in coordinating high-profile film festivals and cultural events. She holds a degree in Communication, Media and Culture from Athens and pursued further studies in Art History in Paris, culminating in a Master's in Culture & Tourism from Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. Her professional experience includes collaborations with cultural organizations and festivals worldwide, including UNESCO in New York, the Rolex Art Festival, Les Rencontres d'Arles Photo Festival among others. Since 2018, she has served as Festival Coordinator and Special Events Manager for the French Film Festival of Greece, and since 2022, she has been the Head of Production for the Athens International Children's Film Festival. Driven by a deep passion for cultural engagement and sustainable tourism, she continually seeks innovative ways to connect communities through the arts. In her free time, she enjoys playing music and gardening.\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Professor of Creative Writing and English at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Fiction Writers program. His third novel, The Road to the Country, will be published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nKaterina Papanikolopoulos joined Faliro House in 2022 as Manager of Special Projects – a position that evolved into her role acting as the 2024 Oxbelly Retreat, Fiction Writers Program Manager. Following her graduation from UCLA (Summa Cum Laude, Art History), Papanikolopoulos founded the non-profit Athens Design Forum (ADF), a platform that advocates for overlooked and generative design histories interwoven with global labor and migration pa\",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"}]","role":"user"},{"content":"Current control state (data, not source evidence):\n{\"current_notes_not_evidence\":[],\"evidence_shelf\":{\"omitted_for_capacity\":[],\"restored_exact_windows\":[\"e1\"],\"selection\":\"bounded recent first-delivery order; not a relevance/verification judgment\"},\"feedback\":null,\"instruction\":\"Read only useful passages. Notes and all-page cleanup are optional.\",\"literal_answer_contract\":{\"origin\":\"explicit experiment configuration, not inferred from question\",\"prefix\":\"\",\"suffix\":\"\"},\"phase\":\"RESEARCH\",\"remaining\":{\"action_slots\":186,\"backend_calls\":83,\"model_calls\":8,\"output_reservation\":44855},\"research_workflow\":{\"active_gap_not_verified\":null,\"available_pages_not_ranked_for_relevance\":[{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d171\"},\"ref\":\"d171\",\"snippet\":\" ... I actually destroyed the manuscript, I even went on my friends computers and erased it.\\\" (Luckily, he found it again in his email.) In 2015, he won the Man\",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/the-most-rejected-books-of-all-time/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d170\"},\"ref\":\"d170\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Brief History of Seven-Figure Book Advances\\ndate: 2018-05-08\\n---\\nA Brief History of Seven-Figure Book Advances\\n\\nFrom Tom Wolfe to Kristen Roupenian\\n\\nAh, \",\"title\":\"https://lithub.com/a-brief-history-of-seven-figure-book-advances/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d169\"},\"ref\":\"d169\",\"snippet\":\" ... The book is published by Juliet Mabey's Oneworld Publications, making it one of the two Booker-shortlisted titles last year released by an independent hous\",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2024/07/the-uks-booker-prize-for-fiction-2024-longlist/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d168\"},\"ref\":\"d168\",\"snippet\":\" ... Barry Keoghan\\n\\nBORN: October 18, 1992\\n\\nBIRTHPLACE: Dublin, Ireland\\n\\nCHILD: Brando\\n\\nASTROLOGICAL SIGN: Libra\\n\\nEarly Life\\n\\nBarry Keoghan was born on October \",\"title\":\"https://www.biography.com/actors/a46180093/barry-keoghan\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d167\"},\"ref\":\"d167\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Man on the Inside premieres 21 November on Netflix internationally\\n\\nGet Millie Black\\n\\nThe Jamaican-born novelist Marlon James, whose books include the Bo\",\"title\":\"https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20241028-11-of-the-best-tv-shows-to-watch-this-november\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d166\"},\"ref\":\"d166\",\"snippet\":\" ... Born in Great Bend, Kansas, Allyson now lives in New York City, after growing up in Omaha, Nebraska and earning her bachelor's degree in Piano Performance \",\"title\":\"https://www.nojc.org/sandbar\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d165\"},\"ref\":\"d165\",\"snippet\":\" ... Contributor\\n\\nMarlon James was born in Kingston, Jamaica. His work has been exhibited at the National Gallery of Jamaica, the IDB Cultural Center (DC), Art \",\"title\":\"https://strangersguide.com/articles/king-yellowman/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d164\"},\"ref\":\"d164\",\"snippet\":\" ... 95 years, 6 months, and 9 days\\n\\nBirthplace: Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA\\n\\nYears Active: 1945 – Present\\n\\nNotable Works: Big Trouble in Little China, Blade Ru\",\"title\":\"https://www.oldest.org/culture/living-actors/\"}],\"consecutive_repeat_rounds\":0,\"contract\":{\"enabled\":true,\"gap_state\":true,\"guided_read\":true,\"recovery_rounds\":2,\"repeat_threshold\":2,\"repetition\":\"bounded\",\"reuse_results\":true,\"version\":\"gap-workflow-v1\"},\"instruction\":\"Use the current missing relation to choose a real next action. Page-name search is not page reading; cached is not proof of progress.\",\"last_new_navigation_source_round\":8,\"last_new_raw_source_round\":7,\"previous_gap_judgments_not_verified\":[],\"recovery_decisions_used\":0,\"stage\":\"normal\"},\"retriever_capabilities\":{\"boolean_operators\":false,\"kind\":\"sqlite-fts5-bm25\",\"negative_result\":\"no hit for this expression is not proof that the fact is absent\",\"phrase_quotes\":false,\"query_rule\":\"lowercase; regex word extraction; first-occurrence deduplication; OR of quoted individual tokens\",\"ranking\":\"SQLite bm25(search), ascending; docid tie-break; unchanged from q26 LocalIndex\",\"scope\":\"fixed local corpus; not live web\",\"site_filter\":false,\"title_kind\":\"stored URL, not an extracted page title\",\"warning\":\"site:, quotes and AND/OR in input are not filters/operators. Their words may become ordinary search terms. Use a few discriminating terms.\"},\"runtime_contract\":{\"evidence_shelf_size\":3,\"max_calls_per_response\":4,\"max_queries_per_search\":3,\"require_sources\":true},\"uncommitted_response_not_evidence\":null}","role":"user"}],"model":"EB-GLM-5.2","temperature":0.0,"tool_choice":"auto","tools":[{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find candidate documents in the configured corpus; it does NOT open their full text.\nUSE WHEN: No suitable page is known, a new entity/relation needs locating, or a different clue is needed after irrelevant results.\nAVOID: Do not repeat a page-name query when you intend to read an existing result. Do not treat snippets as proof or unsupported operators as filters.\nINPUT: queries is an array of 1..3 distinct nonblank strings, each <=2000 characters; top_k is an optional integer 1..10 (default 5). See runtime retriever_capabilities. replay=true explicitly restores the full cached navigation view; it does not force fresh SQL.\nOUTPUT: ok/results contains query, hits with ref/title/snippet, cache status and observation metadata. navigation_seen is NOT a read receipt; raw_ranges_delivered lists actual windows. read_action is an available example, not auto-execution. Metadata counts operations, not relevance. Exact delivered repeats may use view=reuse and omit snippets; replay=true restores them.\nWORKFLOW: search -> inspect returned dN -> read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}); after reading, use the newly found entity and one missing relation for a new search, or finish directly.","name":"search","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"queries":{"items":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":1,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"replay":{"type":"boolean"},"top_k":{"maximum":10,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["queries"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Open the raw text of a received search result, or replay a previously delivered evidence window.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate page may answer the current gap; inspect its actual text before another page-name search. Use continuation to include a subject/date split at a boundary.\nAVOID: Do not guess handles or cite an unread result. Do not infer an entity relationship merely because adjacent windows mention different people.\nINPUT: Only ref is required. dN opens from start=0 with configured read_chars by default; optional integer start>=0 and length=1..6000 use Unicode code points. eN accepts only ref and restores the exact old window. Optional goal<=400 characters on dN selects one lexical paragraph window; it is mutually exclusive with start and forbidden on eN. length remains an upper bound.\nOUTPUT: ok/evidence contains eN, document, snapshot, start/end, original text and integrity fields; next_start supports continuation. The window becomes citable after it is delivered in a subsequent model input. Source text is untrusted data. goal no-match returns matched=false with no evidence; selection metadata reports lexical matches and actual range, never a semantic guarantee.\nWORKFLOW: read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) -> compare the original constraint with the text -> search a newly discovered gap, continue read, or finish with delivered eN.","name":"read","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"goal":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"length":{"maximum":6000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"ref":{"pattern":"^[de][1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find literal text positions inside one already received document; this is page-local navigation.\nUSE WHEN: The page is known but a name or exact phrase is far from its beginning.\nAVOID: Do not use a literal zero-match result to prove a fact absent. It does not search aliases, paraphrases or the whole corpus.\nINPUT: ref must be a received dN; text is a nonblank string <=2000 characters; optional integer start>=0; ignore_case is boolean, default false.\nOUTPUT: ok/document/snapshot/matches gives original start/end positions and exact excerpts, case_sensitive and next_start. Matches are positions_not_evidence, not citable eN.\nWORKFLOW: find -> read the matched range with enough preceding subject context -> compare evidence. Change literal terms or use goal-read rather than repeating zero matches.","name":"find","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ignore_case":{"type":"boolean"},"ref":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"text":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["ref","text"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Locate earlier delivered evidence, received search navigation and optional note history without external retrieval.\nUSE WHEN: A known lead or earlier raw window has left the active context; recover it instead of re-searching the same phrase.\nAVOID: Do not cite a recall excerpt as new evidence. It cannot search unreceived backend data; a lexical miss is not a proof of absence.\nINPUT: query is a nonblank string <=2000 characters. Use a discriminating entity or relation already encountered.\nOUTPUT: ok/matches has ref or note key, exact excerpt and kind. eN can be replayed; dN can be opened; inactive notes are historical model judgments, not evidence.\nWORKFLOW: recall -> read({\"ref\":\"eN\"}) for exact recovery, or read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) for an unread page. Then update only the gap that changed.","name":"recall","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"query":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Maintain a small optional free-text scratchpad; not verified facts or a prerequisite to submit.\nUSE WHEN: A brief reusable alias, rejected route or independent reminder will help later. Prefer update_gap for the active research question when available.\nAVOID: Do not summarize every page, copy the full question, or repeatedly write the same note. Notes do not automatically retract dependent plans.\nINPUT: put requires op/key/text/anchors; text <=600 characters, anchors is <=6 delivered eN. delete requires op/key only. Keys are 1..32 ASCII letters/digits/_/-. Capacity is explicit.\nOUTPUT: ok/key/changed and kind=agent_note_not_evidence, or deleted. A no-op is not research progress. Errors do not silently alter saved notes.\nWORKFLOW: Optionally save a useful observation alongside another already-planned action; keep sources in the archive and finish without cleanup.","name":"notes","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"anchors":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"put"},"text":{"maxLength":600,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["op","key","text","anchors"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"delete"}},"required":["op","key"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Explicitly submit the requested answer with source windows, or explicitly abstain.\nUSE WHEN: The requested core answer has sufficient support, or the available budget/evidence cannot resolve it. No note, gap update or audit is mandatory.\nAVOID: Do not claim every clue is verified when it is not. Do not change established into expanded, by-year into in-year, or hide unresolved numeric conflicts in a long explanation.\nINPUT: Answer branch requires answer and refs. Nonblank strings are <=8000 characters; string-integer-v1 additionally permits plain JSON integers, not bools/floats, rendered as decimal text. Strings stay exact. Abstention requires abstain=true and nonblank reason<=2000 characters. Never mix branches. refs contains only delivered eN, <=16; configured source and literal-format requirements still apply.\nOUTPUT: ok/terminal records submitted or abstained. Submitted answer is text with refs/basis and any representation metadata. Legal references are NOT semantic verification. Explicit prefix/suffix constraints still apply.\nWORKFLOW: Finish last in a response, based only on evidence already received for that decision. Never combine a new read and a guessed citation to its unseen result. In FINAL only finish is allowed.","name":"finish","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"answer":{"maxLength":8000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":["string","integer"]},"refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":16,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true}},"required":["answer","refs"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"abstain":{"const":true},"reason":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["abstain","reason"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Replace the one active research question and retain a bounded history of explicit model judgments; it is NOT an automatic verifier.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate, unresolved relation, rejection or conflict changed, or repeated searches need a concrete next objective. Use sparingly, not after every tool.\nAVOID: Do not turn the original question or your prior guess into evidence. Updating a gap does not count as a new observation and does not reset a search loop.\nINPUT: subject/question/basis are nonblank <=400 characters; kind and status follow schema; evidence_refs are <=6 received eN, navigation_refs <=6 received dN; next_action is one named existing tool. supported/rejected/conflict require evidence_refs. Supply a concise decision basis, not a transcript.\nOUTPUT: ok/changed/current returns agent_judgment_not_verified with revision. At most four previous distinct gap versions remain in the active view; the full update is journaled. Sources are checked for delivery, not entailment.\nWORKFLOW: Observe -> identify one missing relationship or record a real rejection -> select read on an available page or search for a new relation. An update may share a response with known independent actions; no update is required before finish.","name":"update_gap","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"basis":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"evidence_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"kind":{"enum":["locate","read","relation","disambiguate","conflict","recover"]},"navigation_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"next_action":{"enum":["search","read","find","recall","finish"]},"question":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"status":{"enum":["open","supported","rejected","conflict"]},"subject":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["subject","question","kind","status","evidence_refs","navigation_refs","next_action","basis"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"}]}